## Output Format

Each call returns a plain text block like this:

```
Site-7

Category-1
• [specific operational content]
• [specific operational content]

Category-2
• [specific operational content]
• [specific operational content]

...

Category-6
• [specific operational content]
• [specific operational content]
```

---

## How Outputs Are Assembled in the Flow

Inside the `Apply to each` loop, after each Summarizer call, the flow appends the site summary to the `SITE_SUMMARIES` string variable using an `Append to string variable` step. The value appended uses `body/lastResponse` from the agent step:

```
concat(outputs('Execute_Summarizer_Agent_and_wait')?['body/lastResponse'], decodeUriComponent('%0A%0A'))
```

The `decodeUriComponent('%0A%0A')` adds two line breaks between site summaries for readability.

After the loop completes, `SITE_SUMMARIES` contains all site summaries concatenated in the order they appeared in `SiteList`.

---

## Loop Configuration

**Apply to each input:** `SiteList` from the Parse JSON step.
**Concurrency:** Set to 1 (sequential) to prevent the async loop hang. See `docs/architecture/lessons-learned.md` — "The Async Loop Hang."
**Timeout on Execute Agent step:** Extend to `PT5M` (5 minutes) in the Settings tab to give each call sufficient time for sites with large amounts of source content.
